// Canonical source: after new, the reader takes a field, a call with no
// arguments and a call with arguments, each step on what the one before
// answers, so new E().p.v reads a field of a field.
// Answer: 38 (5 + 3 + 10 + 20).
class P : Object { section [public] { int v; P() { this.v = 20; } } }
class E : Object { section [public] { int a; P p; E() { this.a = 5; this.p = new P(); } int M() { return 3; } int Twice(int n) { return n + n; } } }
return new E().a + new E().M() + new E().Twice(5) + new E().p.v;
